Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Clipboard: keyboard scrolling, Pin/Edit/Delete menu,
 menu below the fold

Arrow keys no longer lose the selection to the mouse. Keyboard scrolling
slid rows under a resting cursor and hover selected them; hover now
waits for the pointer to move again after an arrow press.

Pressing Up on the newest item keeps it selected instead of clearing
the selection and showing the empty preview.

The right-click (and Shift+Enter) menu is now just Pin, Edit and
Delete. Edit is the former Alias option; clicking or Enter still copies.

Scroll and hit-testing use the rows' real positions. Rows start at
originY, which moves when new items are inserted on top, so the menu on
a lower item was clamped out of view and clicks on its options counted
as clicks outside it.
